AmiScreamer - benchmark for beta testers
========================================

The benchmark measures how fast AmiScreamer runs on your Amiga. It drives a fixed scene: track 1, a robot drives
400 pictures, detail level 1, no sound, fixed time steps. So the robot drives exactly the same way on every
machine, and the figures can be compared between computers. It measures once at 640x400 and once at 320x200.


Preparation
-----------
1. Install the game with the installation package ("Install!"). Choose your processor (68040, 68060 or 68080).
   Then copy the script "Benchmark" and the debug program for your processor (amiscreamer_debug_040, _060 or
   _080) from the drawer AmiScreamer_Debug into the game's drawer. Only the debug programs can measure; the normal
   programs (amiscreamer_060 and so on) have no measuring in them.
2. In the launcher choose an RTG screen (RTG 640x400 or RTG 320x200), not AGA. Close the launcher.
3. Run as little else as possible (no other programs, no network transfers).


Running the benchmark
---------------------
1. Open a Shell and change to the game's drawer, for example:
     CD Work:Screamer
   (with the German CD the drawer is called "Bleifuss")
2. Start the benchmark with the program for your processor:
     Execute Benchmark amiscreamer_debug_060      (68060)
     Execute Benchmark amiscreamer_debug_040      (68040)
     Execute Benchmark amiscreamer_debug_080      (Vampire, 68080)
3. The game starts twice by itself, first at 640x400, then at 320x200. Each time the robot drives a short way and
   the program ends by itself. Please do not press anything until "Done" appears in the Shell. Depending on the
   computer this takes a few minutes.


What to send back
-----------------
The two files from the game's drawer:
  amiscreamer_bench_hi.log     (640x400)
  amiscreamer_bench_lo.log     (320x200)

And please tell us:
  - CPU and clock (for example 68060 at 50 MHz)
  - accelerator card
  - graphics card (for example Picasso IV, CyberVision 64) and Zorro II or Zorro III
  - AmigaOS version and RTG system (Picasso96 or CyberGraphX)
  - anything unusual (picture errors, crash, hang), briefly described


Reading the figures
-------------------
The logs contain lines like:
  phases (ms a picture): game 3.00  backdrop 1.75  geometry 12.61  painting 42.03  rest 4.03  copy 0.03  = 63.47

These are milliseconds per picture, each the mean of 50 pictures:
  game       game logic (driving, opponents, sound control)
  backdrop   sky and backdrop
  geometry   turning the track and the cars into screen positions
  painting   drawing the polygons
  rest       the displays (speedometer, radar, texts)
  copy       copying the finished picture into the graphics card
  = ...      total per picture

1000 divided by the total gives the pictures per second. The first line of each file still includes the loading
and does not count.

The timing uses the E-clock (timer.device, ReadEClock), so the milliseconds are right on every computer,
whatever the CPU's clock.


For comparison
--------------
Vampire V1200 (68080), program amiscreamer_debug_060:    640x400  63.5 ms (about 16 pictures/s)
                                                          320x200  33.2 ms (about 30 pictures/s)
On a real 68060 the copy over the Zorro bus into the graphics card comes on top (column "copy").

Thank you for testing!
